ine paragraph separators), R3.1 (indentation preservation), R4.1 (file and stdin input), R5.1 (-w WIDTH flag)\n     - Additional requirements needed for a working implementation: R1.1 (default 75-char width), R6.1 (-g goal width), R7.1 (word boundaries), R8.1 (space collapsing), R9.1 (-s split-only), R10.1 (-u uniform spacing), R11.1 (-p prefix), R12.1 (-t tagged paragraph), R13.1-R13.4 (exit codes and testing)\n     - Non-goals: crown margin mode (-c), locale-aware line breaking\n   \n   - `cmd/fmt/main.go` (TO CREATE)\n     - Listed in repository files but no source code provided inline, suggesting it needs to be created\n     - Must implement paragraph reformatting with all flags\n   \n   - `cmd/fmt/fmt_test.go` (TO CREATE)\n     - Differential tests using testutils.RunDiffTests with gfmt reference binary\n   \n   - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` (PROVIDED INLINE)\n     - Contains `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` - must be called at start of main()\n     ```go\n     func InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n         c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n         signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n         go func() {\n             <-c\n             os.Exit(0)\n         }()\n     }\n     ```\n   \n   - `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` and `pkg/testutils/build.go` (PROVIDED INLINE)\n     - DiffTest struct with fields: Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n     - RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests)\n     - BuildBinary(t, \".\") compiles cmd package and returns binary path\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only one tool call was made (Read of the SRD file) which succeeded.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand all requirements before implementation\n   - No implementation has been done yet - was interrupted by summary request after the SRD read\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: Massive task prompt containing the full stitch task specification including: role definition, repository file listing, project context (vision, 