{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015nfh3NpDLReHf8kRvtMG8x","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've collected all the files you requested. Here's the complete information:\n\n## File Contents Summary\n\n### 1. **cmd/cat/main.go** (Complete implementation)\nThis is a comprehensive example of flag parsing and file/stdin handling:\n- **Flag parsing**: `parseFlags()` function handles POSIX-style flags with support for combined flags (`-bsA`) and `--` for end-of-flags\n- **stdin fallback**: When no files are provided, defaults to reading from stdin via `args = []string{\"-\"}` (line 32-34)\n- **File/stdin handling**: `catFile()` checks if name is `\"-\"` to read from stdin (line 109), otherwise opens a file\n- **Exit codes**: Sets exitCode to 1 on errors (line 47), exits 0 on success (line 52), and special handling for SIGPIPE (line 43-44)\n- **Error handling**: Formats errors nicely using `formatErr()` for PathError cleanup (line 212-218)\n- **SIGPIPE handling**: Installs SIGPIPE handler via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` (line 29)\n\n### 2. **cmd/cat/cat_test.go** (Complete test file)\nShows the differential testing pattern with `testutils`:\n- **BuildBinary**: Compiles the Go binary for testing (line 20)\n- **Reference binary**: Uses `gcat` as reference binary for comparison (line 21-24)\n- **DiffTest structure**: Array of test cases with Name, Args, Stdin fields (lines 25-41)\n- **RunDiffTests**: Runs all tests comparing Go binary against reference (line 42)\n- **Additional tests**: Shows other patterns like file handling (TestDiffFiles), error cases (TestMissingFile), and SIGPIPE handling (TestSIGPIPE)\n\n### 3. **pkg/testutils/difftest.go** (Complete utility file)\nThe core differential testing harness:\n- **DiffTest struct** (lines 46-55): Contains Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n- **RunDiffTests function** (lines 83-90): Main entry point that runs subtests comp